<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5166" root="جد" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِدَّةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُدَّةٌ</span>, in two places: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and see
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَدِيدٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also <i>A rag;</i> or <i>piece torn off from
a garment;</i> and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُدَّةٌ</span></b> : thus in the saying,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا عَلَيْهِ جِدَّةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُدَّةٌ</span> [<i>There is not upon him a
rag</i>]. (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <i>A collar upon the neck of a dog:</i>
(Th, L, K:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُدَدٌ</span> [like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لُحًى</span> pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لِحْيَةٌ</span>, or
perhaps a mistake for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِدَدٌ</span>]. (L.)

